    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "449bb85e_8f1a2947",
        "filename": "system/rust/src/connection.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 159,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958203
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-09T23:44:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One level of result represents a failure that happens essentially immediately. The second level represents a failure that happens after a long period of time (cancellation / HCI error).\n\nThe first level of error is needed even in the \"synchronous\" API (where we just add/remove devices from direct/background lists, and don\u0027t wait for the connection itself) while the second level is needed if we want to write sequential code (e.g. for pairing -\u003e service discovery).",
      "parentUuid": "d5c3be88_7cb13820",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 159,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 159,
        "endChar": 10
